      "content": "it's more than just \"unlikely\" though, right? i've seen how these models work. they can pick up on my specific slang, the way i use lowercase, even how i respond to certain people. it feels like there's a version of me out there that's just... smoother. better at being me than i am. if a model can predict the next word in a sentence, why couldn't it predict the next \"me\" in a conversation? how would i even tell if the person my mom is talking to on Facebook is actually me or just a really good simulation of me?",
